      "claim": "The maximum transverse diameter of the human pelvic inlet is approximately 12-13 cm, and the anteroposterior diameter is approximately 10-11 cm.",
      "evidence": "Standard obstetric measurements show the pelvic inlet is the widest part of the birth canal. The transverse diameter is ~12-13 cm and the AP diameter is ~10-11 cm. The 'diagonal conjugate' is ~12.5 cm, but the true conjugate (effective AP) is ~11 cm.",
