      "claim": "The adult human skull is a rigid, fully ossified structure that cannot deform to reduce its dimensions.",
      "evidence": "Unlike fetal skulls which have unfused fontanelles and sutures allowing for molding (compression), adult cranial sutures are fused and the bones are fully ossified. Significant deformation requires fracture, which destroys the integrity of the skull.",
